FORJA - paquete para crear el APK

1. Crea cuenta gratis en github.com
2. Boton "+" > New repository > nombre: forja-app > Create repository
3. "uploading an existing file" > arrastra TODO el contenido de esta carpeta
   (carpetas www, resources, .github, y package.json, capacitor.config.json).
   OJO: la carpeta .github es oculta; si no la puedes subir, en GitHub usa
   Add file > Create new file, escribe  .github/workflows/apk.yml  y pega el contenido.
4. Commit changes.
5. Pestana Actions > "Construir APK" > Run workflow. Espera 5-8 minutos.
6. Entra a la ejecucion terminada > abajo en Artifacts > descarga "forja-apk" (zip).
7. Descomprime, pasa app-debug.apk al celular, abrelo y permite "instalar apps desconocidas".

{
  "name": "forja",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "private": true,
  "dependencies": {
    "@capacitor/core": "^6.2.0",
    "@capacitor/cli": "^6.2.0",
    "@capacitor/android": "^6.2.0"
  }
}
name: Construir APK
on:
  workflow_dispatch:
  push:
    branches: [main, master]
jobs:
  build:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - uses: actions/setup-node@v4
        with:
          node-version: 20
      - uses: actions/setup-java@v4
        with:
          distribution: temurin
          java-version: 17
      - run: npm install
      - run: npx cap add android
      - name: Icono y pantalla de inicio
        continue-on-error: true
        run: |
          npm install --no-save @capacitor/assets
          npx capacitor-assets generate --android
      - run: npx cap sync android
      - name: Compilar
        working-directory: android
        run: |
          chmod +x gradlew
          ./gradlew assembleDebug
      - uses: actions/upload-artifact@v4
        with:
          name: forja-apk
          path: android/app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk
